# Events & Input

## Key Events {: .col-2}

### Characters

```elixir
{:key, {:char, "a"}}        # printable character
{:key, {:char, "ñ"}}        # UTF-8 supported
```

### Named Keys

```elixir
{:key, :enter}
{:key, :tab}
{:key, :escape}
{:key, :backspace}
{:key, :delete}
{:key, :insert}
{:key, :home}
{:key, :end}
{:key, :page_up}
{:key, :page_down}
```

### Arrow Keys

```elixir
{:key, :arrow_up}
{:key, :arrow_down}
{:key, :arrow_left}
{:key, :arrow_right}
```

### Function Keys

```elixir
{:key, :f1}   {:key, :f2}   {:key, :f3}
{:key, :f4}   {:key, :f5}   {:key, :f6}
{:key, :f7}   {:key, :f8}   {:key, :f9}
{:key, :f10}  {:key, :f11}  {:key, :f12}
```

### Modifier Combinations

```elixir
{:key, {:ctrl, "a"}}        # Ctrl+A (lowercase)
{:key, {:alt, "x"}}         # Alt+X
{:key, {:shift, :tab}}      # Shift+Tab

# Modifiers on named keys (sorted list)
{:key, :arrow_up, [:ctrl]}
{:key, :home, [:shift]}
{:key, :f1, [:alt, :ctrl]}
```

Modifier atoms: `:shift`, `:alt`, `:ctrl`, `:super`, `:hyper`

## Mouse Events {: .col-2}

### Button Press & Release

```elixir
{:mouse, :press, :left, col, row}
{:mouse, :release, :left, col, row}
{:mouse, :press, :middle, col, row}
{:mouse, :press, :right, col, row}

# With modifiers
{:mouse, :press, :left, col, row, [:ctrl]}
```

Coordinates are 1-indexed (col, row).

### Scroll

```elixir
{:mouse, :scroll_up, col, row}
{:mouse, :scroll_down, col, row}

# With modifiers
{:mouse, :scroll_up, col, row, [:shift]}
```

## Other Events

### Focus, Paste, Resize

```elixir
# Terminal focus
{:focus, :in}               # terminal gained focus
{:focus, :out}              # terminal lost focus

# Bracketed paste markers
{:paste, :start}
{:paste, :end}

# Terminal resize
{:resize, cols, rows}

# Cursor position response
{:cursor_position, row, col}
```

## Handling Events {: .col-2}

### handle_event/2

Define in any `LiveComponent` to handle input. Return `{:noreply, assigns}`.

```elixir
defmodule MyComponent do
  use Courgette.LiveComponent

  def handle_event({:key, :arrow_up}, assigns) do
    {:noreply, update(assigns, :count, &(&1 + 1))}
  end

  def handle_event({:key, {:char, "q"}}, assigns) do
    Courgette.stop()
    {:noreply, assigns}
  end

  def handle_event(_event, assigns) do
    {:noreply, assigns}
  end
end
```

### Focus Routing

Tab and Shift-Tab are intercepted by the root component to cycle focus between children.

```elixir
# These are handled automatically:
{:key, :tab}                # focus next child
{:key, {:shift, :tab}}      # focus previous child

# Children receive these atoms on focus change:
:focus                      # component gained focus
:blur                       # component lost focus
```

Other events are routed to the currently focused child.

### handle_info/2

Handle arbitrary messages sent to the component process.

```elixir
def handle_info(:tick, assigns) do
  {:noreply, update(assigns, :elapsed, &(&1 + 1))}
end

def handle_info({:child_crashed, {mod, id}, reason}, assigns) do
  # Notified when a child crashes
  {:noreply, assigns}
end
```

## Test Helpers {: .col-2}

### Mounting

```elixir
use Courgette.ComponentTestHelpers

# Defaults: 80x24, empty assigns
view = mount(MyComponent)

# With options
view = mount(MyComponent,
  initial_assigns: %{count: 5},
  width: 120,
  height: 40
)
```

### Sending Events

```elixir
send_event(view, {:key, :arrow_up})
send_event(view, {:key, {:char, "a"}})
send_event(view, {:mouse, :press, :left, 10, 5})

# Convenience helpers
send_tab(view)
send_shift_tab(view)

# Arbitrary messages to handle_info/2
send_info(view, :my_message)
```

All event functions are synchronous — they block until the component processes the event.

### Rendering & Assertions

```elixir
# All text content as a string
assert render_text(view) =~ "Count: 5"

# Raw element tree for structural assertions
tree = render_tree(view)
assert tree.type == :box
assert length(tree.children) == 3
```

### Full Example

```elixir
defmodule CounterTest do
  use ExUnit.Case
  use Courgette.ComponentTestHelpers

  test "arrow up increments" do
    view = mount(Counter, initial_assigns: %{count: 0})
    assert render_text(view) =~ "Count: 0"

    send_event(view, {:key, :arrow_up})
    assert render_text(view) =~ "Count: 1"
  end

  test "tab cycles focus" do
    view = mount(MyApp)
    send_tab(view)
    assert render_text(view) =~ "focused"
  end
end
```
